      title: "Food & Dining Out",
      slides: [
        "INTRO|||Food & Dining Out 🍔|||Master ordering food, asking for modifications, and navigating US dining culture.|||Elo: Vamos aprender a pedir comida em restaurantes nos EUA como um nativo!",
        "VOCAB|||Restaurant Vocab 🏷️|||* **Entrée** / **ahn-tray** - Main course in the US (not appetizer!)\n* **Check/Bill** / **chek** - What you ask for at the end\n* **To-go box** / **to-go-box** - Doggy bag for leftovers|||Elo: Lembre-se: 'Entrée' nos EUA é o prato principal!",
        "CONCEPT|||Connected Speech in Ordering 🗣️|||Link your order using natural flow:\n\n> 🗣️ **Connected Speech Phonetics:**\n> * *'I'd like to get'* becomes **'aid-like-tuh-get'**\n> * *'Can I have a'* becomes **'ka-nai-ha-vuh'**|||Elo: 'Can I have a burger' vira 'ka-nai-ha-vuh burger'.",
        "EXAMPLE|||At the Bistro 🍷|||*\"Hi! Can I get a cheeseburger with medium-rare meat and fries on the side?\"*\n\n> 🗣️ **Help Box:**\n> * *'On the side'* = acompanhamento à parte.|||Elo: Pedido perfeito e super natural!",
        "CULTURE|||Tipping Etiquette in the US 🇺🇸|||Tipping 15%-20% is mandatory for table service in America. Server wages depend on it!|||Elo: Deixe sempre 18%-20% de gorjeta para bom serviço.",
        "DRILL|||⚡ Quick Challenge: Ordering Coffee|||The barista asks: *\"What can I get started for you today?\"*\n\n> 🗣️ **Help Box (Your Response):**\n> * *'Can I get an iced oat milk latte, please?'*\n> \n> 🏆 **XP Multiplier:** Say it smoothly with zero pause!|||Elo: Peça seu café com confiança!|||Can I get an iced oat milk latte, please?",
        "ROLEPLAY|||🎭 Diner in Chicago|||You're ordering lunch from server Jack at a classic Chicago diner.\n\n> *\"Ready to order or do you need a few more minutes?\"*\n\n> 🎭 **Challenge:** Order a burger with fries using connected speech (*'ka-nai-get'*).|||Elo: Faça o pedido com clareza para o garçom!",
        "REVIEW|||Dining Unlocked 🏆|||You unlocked 4 essential skills:\n\n1. **US Menu Terminology**\n2. **Connected Speech**: **'ka-nai-get'** flow\n3. **15%-20% Tipping Rules**\n4. **Food Modification Phrasing**|||Elo: Sensacional! Agora você já sabe pedir qualquer refeição em inglês."
      ]
